@startuml medicare_pipeline_flow
skinparam shadowing false
title Medicare Provider Evaluation Data Pipeline - source traceability (EPIC-010-F-007)\nas of 10/6/26

rectangle "Provider collection\n(spine: NPI, entity type, specialty)" as SPINE
rectangle "Part B\nPhysician & Other Practitioners" as PARTB
rectangle "Part D\nPrescribers by Provider and Drug" as PARTD
rectangle "Medicare Coverage Database\n(covered ICD-10 lists -> procedure justification)" as MCD
rectangle "FDA labeling\n(openFDA / DailyMed)" as FDA
rectangle "ICD-10-CM + AHRQ CCSR\n(code set, hierarchy, clinical categories)" as ICD
rectangle "Hospital Enrollments\n(NPI <-> CCN) + POS size" as ENROLL

rectangle "ProviderMedicare\n(per NPI)" as PM
rectangle "SpecialtyMedicare\n(per NUCC code)" as SM
rectangle "Normalized Indication Map\n(proprietary, per indication)" as MAP
rectangle "Job spec (pipeline config, Mongo)\nscope, source list, step DAG + prerequisites" as SPEC #fef9e7

SPINE --> PM
PARTB --> PM
PARTD --> PM
ENROLL --> PM
ICD --> MAP
MCD --> PM : procedure coverage justification
FDA --> MAP : per-product labels\nmatched to canonical indications
MAP --> PM : parent indications
PM --> SM : roll up per NUCC

SPEC ..> MAP : governs (own cadence;\ngated by build_indication_map)
SPEC ..> PM
SPEC ..> SM
note bottom of MAP : hierarchy adopted from ICD-10-CM / CCSR;\nper-product FDA labels matched to the canonical indications.\n"given an indication, best provider"
@enduml
